            <ArticleTitle>Rosuvastatin for cardiovascular prevention: too many uncertainties.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>176</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A randomised trial showed that rosuvastatin had some efficacy in preventing a first cardiovascular event, but there was an increased risk of diabetes. The article describing this study is too imprecise to recommend the use of rosuvastatin in this setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
